{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Status: patchset 2 pushed, second plan-review run in flight\n\nRecording state so the ticket is not the only place this is written down.\n\n**Change 2684, patchset 2** is up and addresses every LLM-Review -1 finding from patchset 1. Note\nthat patchset 1 had earned **`Verified +1`** before being superseded (Gerrit reported the vote as\noutdated on the new push), so CI passed on the same test suite.\n\n**Plan-review gate:** first run BLOCKed (3 findings, all correct, all about the description rather\nthan the code — see the previous comment). Description rewritten. Second run started against the\ncorrected plan and is still executing; `review-plan --status` reports `unsigned`, so the\nattestation is not yet earned. The first run's own telemetry gives the scale:\n`GATE_PEAK_RSS elapsed_ms=289103` — nearly five minutes of gate for a ~237s review, on a box that\nhas been running test suites all session. Not bounding it, per the gate-duration rule.\n\n### What the fix now contains, after review\n\n| finding | change |\n|---|---|\n| truncation hook depended on IMDS — could fail in the failure it reports | guard moved ahead of the prologue; region read from a cache the main run writes; journald first, `aws` only with a validated region |\n| ExecStopPost re-ran the prologue on every stop | fixed by the same move |\n| stop path carried an unbudgeted 3x5s of curls | fixed by the same move, plus explicit `TimeoutStopSec=15` |\n| `du -x --max-depth=1` silently wrong if overlay2 gets its own volume | O(1) st_dev check; subtotal reported unknown on mismatch |\n| a test whose pass condition was not its name | now asserts the grant; the clamp-removal mutation is caught by two tests |\n| source scan called a change-detector | kept, justified, and made robust via an in-tree `# composition-door` marker plus a test pinning the marker count at two |\n\nSix mutations re-run **serially** and all killed. Worth recording why serially: my first sweep\nreported all seven MISSED, which was two of my own errors compounding — the \"caught\" detector\nmatched `^FAILED` against ANSI-coloured output so it never matched, and I had a full `tests/scripts`\nrun executing against the same worktree while the sweep was mutating files in it. Both results were\ngarbage. Neither was a finding about the code. Re-run cleanly, the sweep is unambiguous.\n\n### Open\n\n- Second plan-review run to finish and, if it PASSes, sign the attestation that unblocks the\n  `bugfix-size-attestation` finding.\n- Bots to re-vote `LLM-Review` and `Verified` on patchset 2.\n- Not submitting — that is the operator's call.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788647041426333730,"uuid":"ae4ae8d8-7eab-46ef-a528-4afe680939fb"}